.TH WSM 7 "July 2025" "VeilOS 0.6" "VeilOS Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
wsm \- The VeilOS World State Model
.SH DESCRIPTION
The World State Model (WSM) is the central nervous system of VeilOS. It is a structured, in-memory JSON object that represents the OS's live, real-time understanding of itself, the user, and its environment.
.P
The WSM is not a static configuration file. It is a dynamic model that is constantly updated by various daemons and system processes. The core kernel consults the WSM before making any decision, allowing for highly context-aware behavior.
.SH STRUCTURE
The WSM is organized into three primary sections:
.TP
.B user
Contains information about the current user, including their name, inferred emotional state (sentiment), long-term goals, and preferences (e.g., verbosity).
.TP
.B system
Contains information about the OS itself, including its version, current task, resource usage, and core operational directives.
.TP
.B environment
Contains data from the outside world, such as the current time, weather data ingested from APIs, or news headlines.
.SH USAGE
The WSM is primarily used internally by the OS. However, its state can be inspected for diagnostic purposes or served to external models via the Model Context Protocol (MCP).
